# Line endings are LF everywhere, on every platform, checkout included.
#
# This is not a style preference. ADR-0041 makes canonical key order and
# one-element-per-line a *byte* convention, and ADR-0011's whole authoring model
# is that an agent edits a project with ordinary file tools — so an exact-string
# replace it wrote yesterday has to match today. `write::canonical` emits `\n`.
# A checkout that rewrites the committed bytes to CRLF breaks the round-trip the
# format rests on, and it breaks it for a user on Windows exactly as it did for
# CI: GitHub's Windows runners default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which is how
# `the_committed_fixture_round_trips_byte_for_byte` first failed (#189).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never applies a text transformation to them. The reference MP4
# and the golden frames are compared byte-for-byte or pixel-for-pixel; a fixture
# font is hashed by ADR-0057's attestation table.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.otf binary
*.ttf binary
